      "title_at_revision": "Glide (Single-engined aeroplanes)",
      "text": "The maximum horizontal distance travelled in still air, in km per 1000 m (nautical miles per 1 000 ft) of altitude lost in a glide, and the speed necessary to achieve this, must be determined with the engine inoperative and its propeller in the minimum drag position, landing gear and wing flaps in the most favourable available position.",
